<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xu Wen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">862–927</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Xu Wen was a general of the Wu kingdom of the Ten Kingdoms period. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yang-xingmi">Yang Xingmi</a>'s death he seized control of the government from the weak Yang heirs and ruled as regent, while his adopted son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-bian">Xu Zhigao</a> ran affairs from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Jinling</a>; in 937 Xu Zhigao took the throne and founded the Southern Tang.</p></div>
